Hi, I'm Bob Vila. Welcome to This Old House. In a few minutes, I'm going to show you our new This Old House, but before I do, we've got some unfinished business here. As you know, this place, the Bigelow House, was the site of our second restoration. We turned an abandoned country estate into five condominium residences.

00:00:49.800 --> 00:00:56.240
The good news is that two of the units, the barn and the stable, have been sold for about the price we wanted.

00:00:57.800 --> 00:00:59.980
The bad news is that the remaining...

00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:05.320
three units have not sold. The main house, our spacious four-bedroom unit, is available

00:01:05.320 --> 00:01:12.960
for $400,000. The woodshed with that nice country kitchen is on the market for $250,000.

00:01:13.140 --> 00:01:18.260
And the ice house, one of my favorite units with all the skylights up above, is available

00:01:18.260 --> 00:01:23.450
for $210,000. You know, when we started the Bigelow house, there was really a large market

00:01:23.450 --> 00:01:29.980
for luxury housing. But in the meantime, interest rates shot up so that owners...

00:01:30.000 --> 00:01:35.960
can't afford to sell and buyers can't afford to buy. So here we sit. Like many others,

00:01:36.140 --> 00:01:40.680
we're writing out these hard times and we're trying to develop some creative financing

00:01:40.680 --> 00:01:46.290
that will make these condos more affordable. But all that aside, let's go take a look now

00:01:46.290 --> 00:01:52.550
at the new This Old House. Our new This Old House is located just north of the city of Boston

00:01:52.550 --> 00:01:58.510
in Woburn, Massachusetts. Woburn is a city of 34,000 inhabitants on 13 square miles of land.

00:01:58.760 --> 00:01:59.880
for our purposes.

00:02:00.000 --> 00:02:05.030
Woburn is ideal. It is a mature community with all of the city services one would ever need.

00:02:05.360 --> 00:02:10.020
It's always had enough industry and manufacturing to provide jobs for its residents, as well as

00:02:10.020 --> 00:02:15.040
being close to the central city and shopping. But more importantly, it's one of those communities

00:02:15.040 --> 00:02:20.040
that still has affordable housing. While Woburn may not be the most fashionable place to live,

00:02:20.380 --> 00:02:27.160
for value in housing, you can't beat it. Well, let's take a look at our new neighborhood.

00:02:27.640 --> 00:02:29.980
You know, 25 years ago, this was acres and acres of...

00:02:30.000 --> 00:02:34.960
rolling New England farmland, pasture probably with black and white cows dotting the landscape.

00:02:35.400 --> 00:02:42.080
And about that time, 1956, the developer bought the land. He decided there was an urgent need for

00:02:42.080 --> 00:02:46.700
single-family housing for that whole post-World War II generation that was starting their own

00:02:46.700 --> 00:02:54.430
families. And he decided to build simple ranch houses out here, plan A or plan B. Put up 406 of

00:02:54.430 --> 00:02:58.700
them probably in six months or so. The way they did them was almost like an assembly line because

00:02:58.700 --> 00:02:59.860
They'd come out here, clear the land.

00:03:00.250 --> 00:03:04.710
set up the half-acre parcels, bring in one crew doing foundation, one right after another,

00:03:04.790 --> 00:03:10.080
and they were followed by framing crews and roofing crews, etc. And all these houses back then

00:03:10.080 --> 00:03:16.840
were available for the staggering sum of $13,100. You'd be lucky today to buy a family station

00:03:16.840 --> 00:03:22.500
wagon for that much. Over 25 years, what's happened is that they've been used largely as

00:03:22.500 --> 00:03:26.480
starter homes for many families. Some of them have been owned by three and four different families.

00:03:26.580 --> 00:03:29.980
And what they have done is that they have added a garage or a family

00:03:30.000 --> 00:03:36.870
room or in one way or another altered the original plan a or plan b so that you have a lot more

00:03:36.870 --> 00:03:42.790
interesting looking houses right now but one thing remains the same they're still affordable

00:03:42.940 --> 00:03:49.520
houses around here are selling in the 60s 61 000 65 000 thereabouts they all come with a half acre

00:03:49.520 --> 00:03:56.130
lot and they're all pretty nice little houses let's pull in here and we'll take a closer look at ours

